/.rak200/

# Seeded files, conformance-checked byte for byte or under a mask. A formatter that
# rewrites a seed turns the next CI run red for a reason nobody will guess.
/.github/

# Written by release-please, in release-please's format. Formatting them starts an
# argument with the tool that rewrites them on every release — and the manifest is
# machine state, not source. Measured: the first Release PR opened in this ecosystem
# went red on `prettier --check` over .release-please-manifest.json alone.
/CHANGELOG.md
/.release-please-manifest.json

# A seed, conformance-checked byte for byte. A formatter that reformats a seed reddens
# the next CI run for a reason nobody will guess — the same reason /.github/ is above.
/release-please-config.json

